{"nodes": [{"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "label": "Chat multi-frontend sample", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Demonstrates the framework as a real distributed system - clustered, sharded, persistent, live-broadcasting - paired with six frontends on one protocol so their feel can be compared side by side."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chatroomactor", "label": "ChatRoomActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One sharded PersistentActor per room. Snapshots every 100 events mean a room with 10k messages cold-starts in the cost of ~100 events read, independent of total history length."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_httpingressactor", "label": "HttpIngressActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs as a ClusterSingleton so exactly one node binds the public port; a survivor re-binds on failure, giving users one URL and no per-node ports without any external load balancer. Non-holders stay warm running persistence, shards, pubsub and presence."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chatroomdirectoryactor", "label": "ChatRoomDirectoryActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wraps a DistributedData ORSet so runtime-created rooms converge across nodes while the default-room seed stays idempotent; room names are validated to the same shape as Memcached/filesystem keys on both sides."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_directmessagechannelactor", "label": "DirectMessageChannelActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DMs are modelled as virtual @username rooms so no new protocol frames are needed; the existing send/join/message/history frames carry them and the server routes by the leading @."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_onlineusersactor", "label": "OnlineUsersActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A DistributedData ORSet per room tracking who is currently connected."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_readreceiptsactor", "label": "ReadReceiptsActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A DistributedData LWWMap of username to highest acknowledged timestamp, with a monotonic guard so a stale write cannot roll a user's pointer backwards; for DMs the entry is keyed on the canonical pair id so both participants share one view."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_usersessionactor", "label": "UserSessionActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One actor per WebSocket connection, owning that client's session."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_websocket_protocol", "label": "Shared WebSocket chat protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All client traffic - login, room list, history, presence, typing, receipts - flows through a single /ws endpoint with no REST, which is what lets six independently built frontends share one contract."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_cluster_port_auto_discovery", "label": "Cluster port auto-discovery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each node walks the port range from 2551, claims the first free port and treats every occupied port below it as a seed, so three identical commands form a cluster with no flags; explicit --port/--seeds remain for cross-machine deployments where a same-host scan cannot work."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_canonical_pair_id", "label": "canonicalPairId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both orderings of a user pair map to one id, so a DM resolves to a single sharded entity. Each user subscribes once at login to their own inbox topic, so every DM lands there regardless of conversation and the client keeps no per-channel subscription bookkeeping."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_typing_indicators", "label": "Typing indicators", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ephemeral-PubSub demonstration: broadcast through the room's existing topic with no persistence and no actor in between. The server filters self-echoes; the client debounces outbound to one per half second and clears stale indicators after three seconds."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_session_tokens", "label": "HMAC session tokens and scrypt passwords", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Passwords are scrypt salt:hash verified with timingSafeEqual, and credential validation scans every user - verifying against a real hash even on a username miss - so timing does not leak enumeration. Tokens self-validate without a lookup; the replicated map stores only revocations, and reconnect-resume reauthenticates a client across a singleton failover."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_smoke_test", "label": "smoke-test.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single-node by design, to isolate the protocol round-trip from the cluster's lazy shard-allocation timing so it stays deterministic. --spawn-backend brings up its own node on ports outside the auto-discovery window, so a self-spawned run neither joins nor collides with a live cluster - and that is how CI runs it."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_failover_test", "label": "failover-test.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spawns three nodes, finds the port owner via the OS port table, kills it and verifies a different PID picks up the bind and serves HTTP. Deliberately not in the CI example gate: two of its three backends were observed outliving a clean exit and holding their cluster ports, poisoning whatever ran next."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_tls_wss", "label": "TLS and WSS support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frontends auto-promote ws to wss from location.protocol, so one cert/key pair flips the whole stack without any client change; production is expected to terminate TLS at a reverse proxy, with the flags there for setups where the process owns the public listener."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_production_hardening", "label": "Production hardening gaps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CSRF/origin checks, login rate limiting and a real user store are config-driven through existing middleware slots rather than deeper code changes, so the demo points at the wiring shape instead of duplicating it."}, {"id": "examples_chat_readme_chat_frontend_matrix", "label": "Six frontend variants", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Plain HTML, Angular, React+Vite, Next.js, SvelteKit and Lit, each building into static/<framework>/ and served by the static plugin - a direct comparison of stacks over one identical protocol."}], "edges": [{"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chatroomactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_httpingressactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chatroomdirectoryactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_directmessagechannelactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_onlineusersactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_readreceiptsactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_usersessionactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_cluster_port_auto_discovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_chat_sample", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chat_frontend_matrix", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_usersessionactor", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chat_websocket_protocol", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_httpingressactor", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chat_websocket_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "examples/chat/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "examples_chat_readme_usersessionactor", "target": "examples_chat_readme_chatroomactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_sc